  "slug": "phenotype-biomedical-corpus-b5a5",
  "summary": "Recent preprints test whether LLM agents keep biomedical conclusions traceable to source documents and evidence rather than free generation.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is LLM agents whose outputs are constrained by explicit evidence sources rather than free generation. LibStructBench tests whether agents exactly reconstruct sequencing-library structures from source documents, while DeepMAST describes an evidence-governed multi-agent system using MCP tools and RAG for traceable spatial transcriptomics analysis. GLESKit links gene-level databases, tools and literature into retained workspaces for reviewable reports. Evaluation against source material is central to several items: EDB-Bio probes whether language models weigh biological evidence across drug transcriptomics, CRISPR screens and GWAS episodes, and SMART tests whether scRNA-seq cancer findings transfer across six cancer types in 121 studies. The harness item attributes hypothesis-generation quality to the prompting harness rather than model tier. What is new is the joint emphasis on evidence governance and evaluation against source material, rather than retrieval alone.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-30"
}
